sava-onnx
ONNX conversions of Inworld SAVA, by github.com/Robinbinu (huggingface.co/Binu30).
Unofficial: not made, reviewed or endorsed by Inworld AI.

Changes from the original work (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):
- The SAVA weights (inworld/sava, sava.safetensors) are exported to ONNX as
  offline and streaming graphs, unchanged except for numeric format: fp32, fp16
  weight storage, and dynamic int8 quantization of some matrix multiplications.
- For export only, the mel frontend's strided unfold is computed as an
  equivalent convolution, and sliding-window attention runs as one masked pass
  instead of 512-frame chunks. Outputs match the original within 5e-6 (fp32).
- sava_onnx/__init__.py ports inworld/sava/segmenter.py and the Session/run API
  to numpy and ONNX Runtime.
